\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Python for Everybody with AI: My Second Campus-Linked Open Course\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs24 \cf0 Learn Python first. Then learn Python with AI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b \cf0 TL;DR:
\f2\b0  I'm launching 
\f0\b Python for Everybody with AI
\f2\b0  on January 1, 2027. It's a new course where students first learn Python without AI, then learn to use AI to solve increasingly sophisticated programming problems. It's my second Campus-Linked Open Course (CLOC), combining the flexibility of online learning with the schedule, office hours, and human support of a live University of Michigan course. Our first CLOC, teaching Django, is already underway and going well. The course costs $300, includes up to 360 days of access, and is open to learners anywhere in the world.\

\f0\b Learn more or enroll: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://python.dr-chuck.com/?utm=linkedin2"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 https://python.dr-chuck.com}}
\f2\b0 \
Since 1997, I've been working to make programming education accessible to anyone, anywhere in the world. Over those nearly 30 years, the technology has changed dramatically, from early web-based courses to MOOCs and now AI. But the fundamental challenge remains the same: how do we help people not just access educational materials, but actually succeed at learning?\
My Python for Everybody materials have now reached more than 10 million learners through Coursera, edX, freeCodeCamp, FutureLearn, and hundreds of schools and universities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 In January 2027, I'm launching a new version of the course: 
\f0\b Python for Everybody with AI
\f2\b0 , offered as a Campus-Linked Open Course (CLOC).\
This is my second CLOC. The first, 
\f0\b Building Web Applications in Django
\f2\b0 , is currently running alongside my University of Michigan course, and I'm encouraged by what we're learning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What is a CLOC?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 A Campus-Linked Open Course occupies a space between a traditional Massive Open Online Course (MOOC) and formal university enrollment.\
MOOCs provide wonderful access to educational content, but learners are often on their own. They watch videos, complete assignments, and try to stay motivated without much human interaction.\
A university course offers a different experience: a calendar, classmates, regular communication, instructors, office hours, and a sense that something is happening 
\f1\i right now
\f2\i0 .\
A CLOC brings some of that university experience to online learners without requiring formal enrollment.\
CLOC learners follow the campus course calendar, receive weekly communication, and participate in live help sessions and office hours. They have a cohort of fellow learners moving through the material at roughly the same time.\
But there are no required examinations, grades, or late penalties. If life gets busy, learners can slow down and continue at their own pace for up to 360 days.\
The goal is simple: 
\f0\b flexible online learning with the rhythm, community, and human support of an active university course.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Our first CLOC is working\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 In September 2026, we launched our first CLOC, Building Web Applications in Django, alongside my undergraduate SI-357 course at the University of Michigan School of Information.\
We have 20 online learners in this first offering. Some are keeping pace with the campus course, while others are moving more slowly. Many have been coming to my office hours.\
One learner described the experience this way:\
"One of the best things about this CLOC-357 is that it doesn't feel like just another online course."\
Another appreciated having the pace of a college course while retaining the option to spread the work over an entire year.\
We are still learning and improving the model, but the important thing is that the CLOC is no longer just a proposal. We are teaching one right now, interacting with real students from around the world, and seeing how the campus connection changes the online learning experience.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Why Python for Everybody with AI?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 My original Python for Everybody course will remain AI-free. There are excellent reasons to learn programming without AI assistance, and I want that option to remain available.\
But I also believe students should learn how to use AI effectively as part of becoming skilled programmers.\
The new course follows a deliberate sequence:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Learn Python fundamentals without AI.
\f2\b0  Build the ability to read, write, and understand programs independently.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Demonstrate those fundamentals without AI.
\f2\b0 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Learn Python again, this time with AI.
\f2\b0  Discover how AI can help with programming, debugging, explanation, and problem solving.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Apply Python and AI together to increasingly sophisticated problems.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This is not a course in "vibe coding" where students simply ask AI to generate programs they don't understand.\
I want students to develop real programming skills first, then use AI to extend what they can accomplish.\
My hope is that someone who begins with absolutely no programming experience can finish this course able to tackle surprisingly advanced problems using Python and AI together.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Join us in January 2027\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Python for Everybody with AI begins January 1, 2027, and follows the Winter semester schedule at the University of Michigan School of Information.\
The cost is 
\f0\b $300
\f2\b0 , which helps support the instructional staff who provide live help and interact with learners. CLOC students are not formally enrolled at the University of Michigan and do not receive university credit or a transcript.\
I am excited to bring this approach to Python for Everybody. After years of providing free educational content, I want to explore how we can make the 
\f1\i process of learning
\f2\i0  more accessible too.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

